  "ref": "DEU.13.11",
  "review_notes": [
    "*any such wickedness as this is* is divided by counting the ASV's determiners against the phrase's morphemes: *any* to the article of דָּבָר, *this* to the demonstrative pronoun, *such ... as* to the comparative כְּ, with the two agreement articles unrepresented.",
    "*wickedness* is read as one rendering of דָּבָר הָרָע under rule 30; the alternative gives it to רָע alone and marks דָּבָר unrepresented, which rule 30 forbids."
  ]
